          "text": "completeness_of_public_minor_league_injured_list_data",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1/claim/27",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Late-game defensive substitution. Owner: manager and bench coach. Decision: replace a weaker defender with a stronger one when leading late, many games per season. Cases: every club makes this choice, or passes on it, routinely, so league-wide cases are numerous. Outcome: subsequent defensive plays, the lost bat if the game is tied or extended, and the result, all publicly observable. Baseline: substitute when leading by a small margin in the final innings. Intervention: a per-situation estimate trading expected defensive runs saved over the remaining outs against the expected offensive loss if the substitute's spot comes up again, including extra-innings probability.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1/claim/28",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Fails (c) possibly, because the remaining outs are few, so value per decision is small and only adds up if the baseline is badly miscalibrated.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1/claim/29",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Fails (a) partly, because the substitute's defensive impact over a few outs is mostly unobservable noise; tests must rely on modeled defensive value.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1/claim/30",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "whether_current_league_practice_differs_measurably_from_model_break_even",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1/claim/31",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Manager replay challenges on non-ball-strike plays. Owner: replay coordinator and manager. Decision: challenge or not on close plays at the bases, tag plays and catches, multiple opportunities per game. Cases: challenges occur league-wide many times per season and outcomes are published, so cases are numerous. Outcome: overturned, confirmed or stands, publicly reported. Baseline: challenge whenever the video room's confidence crosses a gut threshold, with conservative behavior early in games. Intervention: a break-even model combining overturn probability, the play's run or win-expectancy swing, the inning and the option value of retaining the challenge.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1/claim/32",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Fails (d) partly, because the key input, the video room's own read, is private, and public data show only challenged plays, not unchallenged close plays.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1/claim/33",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Fails (c) possibly, because overturn value is concentrated in a small number of high-leverage plays per club-season.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1/claim/34",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Overlaps conceptually with the explored ABS challenge-strategy family; it is distinct only because the inputs are video confidence and play leverage rather than pitch location.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1/claim/35",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "availability_of_unchallenged_close_play_records",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1/claim/36",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Intentional walk decisions after the automatic intentional walk rule. Owner: manager. Decision: issue an intentional walk in base-out and score states where it is possible, several times per month. Cases: league-wide intentional walks and comparable non-walk situations recur each season, so cases are numerous. Outcome: subsequent plate appearances and runs, publicly observable. Baseline: walk the dangerous hitter with first base open late in close games. Intervention: a matchup-specific run- and win-expectancy comparison using the batter and on-deck hitter's pitch-type vulnerabilities against the current pitcher, and the platoon and bench state.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1/claim/37",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Fails (c) likely, because intentional walks are less frequent in modern play, so total value per club may be small.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1/claim/38",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Fails (a) partly, because walks are chosen in non-random situations, which confounds naive retrospective comparisons.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1/claim/39",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/1",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "league_wide_intentional_walk_frequency_trend_since_rule_change",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
