        "whether_public_tracking_records_held_runner_opportunities_consistently",
        "Starting pitcher removal timing within a game. Owner: manager and pitching coach. Decision: remove or continue the starter at each batter boundary from the middle innings onward, every start. Cases: every start league-wide over many seasons, so the number of decision points is far larger than the number of starts. Outcome: the plate-appearance outcomes that follow, publicly observable. Baseline: a pitch-count threshold or times-through-order rule. Intervention: a per-batter estimate of starter-versus-reliever expected run value using within-game velocity and spin decay, upcoming hitter handedness and quality, and the reliever availability already known to the club.",
