        "Infield-in versus infield-back with a runner on third and fewer than two outs. Owner: manager and infield coach. Decision: infield depth on each qualifying plate appearance, many times per season. Cases: the base-out state recurs throughout every season for all clubs, and public tracking includes fielder positioning, so cases are numerous. Outcome: whether the run scored, hit or out, and the batted-ball result, all public. Baseline: infield in late and close, back otherwise. Intervention: a batter- and pitcher-specific ground-ball and exit-velocity model plus runner speed, giving the break-even inning and score for each matchup.",
