          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Problem: individualized hitter approach plans (swing or take by count and pitch zone) against a specific opposing starter. Owner: the hitting coaches. Decision: the pre-game plan for each hitter in each game, made daily. Cases: every plate appearance league-wide, with public pitch-level data on swing decisions. Observable outcome: swing-decision quality and run value per plate appearance against that pitcher type. Baseline: a uniform team approach adjusted only for pitcher handedness. Intervention: plans that match each hitter's demonstrated swing-decision weaknesses to the opposing pitcher's location and count tendencies.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/2/claim/20",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "The retrospective test cannot observe what plan a hitter was given. Only the mismatch between hitter tendencies and pitcher tendencies can be measured, so the test checks for opportunity rather than the effect of the intervention. This is a failure on (b) for the intervention itself.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
