          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "cubs_existing_hitter_plan_process",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/2/claim/24",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Problem: converting minor-league players to new positions (for example shortstop to second base or center field, or position player to pitcher). Owner: the player development director. Decision: whether and when to convert, made a moderate number of times per organization each year. Cases: conversions league-wide are identifiable from public appearance-by-position logs, but they number far fewer than promotions. Observable outcome: defensive metrics at the new position where public, plus offensive trajectory and progression to MLB. Baseline: convert when a player's age-for-level and error or range proxies fall below a threshold. Intervention: a model predicting the defensive value gain from a move using public batted-ball and sprint data.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/2/claim/25",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Enough conversions happen league-wide each season for statistical power. This is likely marginal on (a), and conversions to pitcher may be too rare.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/2/claim/26",
