          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/2",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Problem: choosing which player to take within a draft round, as distinct from the explored bonus-pool allocation. Owner: the scouting director. Decision: hundreds of picks league-wide each year, including about one per round for each club. Cases: many draft classes of public pick lists linked to public pro outcomes. Observable outcome: progress through the minors and MLB value, observed only after many years. Baseline: consensus public prospect rankings. Intervention: a model reweighting public amateur performance data against the consensus.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
