          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "value_per_season_of_throw_target_optimization",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/15",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Problem: runner tag-up and advance decisions on fly balls and balls in the dirt. Owner: baserunning coordinator and first- and third-base coaches. Decision: go or stay, made many times per season. Historical cases: league-wide, every fly ball with a runner on third or second and fewer than two outs, plus pitches in the dirt with runners on. Observable outcome: advance, out, or stay, and the resulting run expectancy. Simple baseline: a fixed rule such as \"tag on any medium-depth fly,\" or current club tendencies. Intervention: opponent-specific go thresholds using catcher block and transfer metrics, outfielder arm and catch-point depth, and runner speed.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/16",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Catcher blocking and outfielder throwing metrics are stable enough within a season to justify thresholds specific to each opponent.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/17",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Runners who stay are not mostly cases where going was obviously wrong, so the comparison is not trivially confounded.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/18",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "This does not substantially overlap already explored stolen-base or baserunner families. That needs a reviewer's check.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/19",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "overlap_with_explored_baserunning_families",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/20",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "public_availability_of_catcher_blocking_inputs",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/21",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Problem: manager replay-challenge decisions on reviewable non-pitch calls such as tag plays, force plays and fair/foul calls. Owner: manager and replay-room staff. Decision: challenge or not, made several times per week per club. Historical cases: league-wide, every published replay review and outcome across seasons. Observable outcome: call overturned or confirmed, and loss of challenge capacity. Simple baseline: challenge whenever the replay room signals \"likely,\" or challenge late-game close plays only. Intervention: a calibration audit of replay-room confidence against overturn outcomes, with challenge thresholds that depend on leverage and challenges remaining.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/22",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Public replay logs include enough play context to estimate leverage. Unchallenged missed calls are mostly unobservable, so criterion (b) is only partly met.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/23",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "The value at stake is meaningful. It may be small relative to other families, so criterion (c) is at risk.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/24",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "The replay room's internal confidence signals could be logged going forward. This is a prospective test, not a retrospective one.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/25",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "public_replay_log_granularity",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/26",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "unchallenged_missed_call_rate",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/27",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Problem: how much weight to give spring-training performance in Opening Day roster and role choices. Owner: front office and major-league staff. Decision: roster spots and roles for marginal players, made once per spring, with several cases per club and many league-wide. Historical cases: league-wide, players with spring data whose roster outcome and following-season performance are public. Observable outcome: regular-season performance and roster survival. Simple baseline: ignore spring stats entirely and rank by projection, or rank by spring surface stats. Intervention: test whether spring tracking data such as velocity, swing speed and contact quality, where publicly captured, adds signal beyond projections.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/28",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Public spring tracking data exists for enough venues and seasons. Coverage gaps may break criteria (a) and (d).",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/29",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Selection bias can be handled. Players who made rosters got playing time and others did not, so outcomes are only observed for those selected.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/30",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Marginal roster spots carry enough value to satisfy criterion (c). This may fail if their replacement-level differences are tiny.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/31",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "spring_tracking_data_public_coverage",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/32",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "UNKNOWN",
          "text": "incremental_signal_over_projection_systems",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/33",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Problem: converting minor-league starters to relievers, or relievers to starters, in player development. Owner: pitching development staff. Decision: role conversion, made several times per season per organization and many times league-wide. Historical cases: league-wide, minor-league pitchers whose role changed, identifiable from public game logs. Observable outcome: later level reached, MLB appearances and performance after the switch. Simple baseline: convert when a pitcher is old for the level and has a fastball-heavy profile or poor stamina. Intervention: a model using public minor-league tracking data and pitch-mix breadth to rank which pitchers are likely to gain from conversion.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/34",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Public minor-league pitch tracking covers enough levels and years to train on.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/35",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Role changes driven by injury or organizational need can be separated from performance-driven conversions. If not, the causal estimate is confounded.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/36",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "Outcomes are observed within a horizon useful to the club. Development lag may delay feedback by several years and weaken criterion (b).",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3/claim/37",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/3",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "This differs enough from the explored call-up translation and pitch design families.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
