          "text": "Affiliate level-to-level promotion timing within the minor leagues (owner: farm director; decision: when to promote a prospect from one minor-league level to the next, dozens of moves per organization-season). Historical cases: thousands of public level changes league-wide in MiLB transaction and stat records. Observable outcome: performance and age-relative-to-level at the new level, and eventual MLB arrival. Simple baseline: promote after a fixed time-at-level or a statistical threshold. Intervention: a public-data hazard model of how hitters and pitchers struggle or adjust after promotion, used to flag prospects who are likely ready early or too late.",
