          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Problem=choosing which regular to rest on which day; owner=manager with performance staff; decision=the daily lineup omission, made most days of the season; historical cases=every starter-absence day league-wide, inferable from public lineups and injury lists; outcome=the team result that day and the rested player's later performance and injured-list placements, all public; baseline=rest players by a fixed cadence, or on day games after night games, or against tough opposing starters; intervention=pick rest days by the expected run cost of the replacement, given the opposing starter's handedness and quality and the bench matchup.",
