          "kind": "IDEA",
          "text": "Problem=intentional walks and unintentional-intentional pitch-around choices; owner=manager and pitching coach; decision=walk or pitch to a batter with a base open, faced several times per week; historical cases=every base-open, late-leverage plate appearance league-wide, with the choice inferable for automatic walks and approximately inferable from pitch location for pitch-arounds; outcome=play result and win-probability change, public; baseline=walk dangerous hitters with first base open late in close games; intervention=a matchup-specific run-expectancy comparison using the next hitter's projection and the platoon state.",
          "status": "UNVERIFIED",
          "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
        },
        {
          "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5/claim/26",
          "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5",
          "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
          "text": "(c) likely fails because public research suggests these decisions carry little value per case, and clubs may have converged on them already; that claim needs verification and is not supplied here.",
