        "(c) likely fails because public research suggests these decisions carry little value per case, and clubs may have converged on them already; that claim needs verification and is not supplied here.",
        "Labeling pitch-arounds from pitch location adds measurement error that could swamp a small effect.",
        "This is included as a deliberate failure case, because (b) fails: warm-up events and pitch counts are not reliably public, so a retrospective test lacks labels even though (a) and (c) may hold.",
        "The idea is viable only with the club's private bullpen logs, which conflicts with the public-data constraint, so it should be parked rather than tested.",
        "This is included as a (c) failure case: public research suggests that optimal and reasonable orders differ by little over a season, and the effect would be undetectable against noise even with strong (a); this needs citation before it is relied on."
