    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/33",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Intentional walk and situational pitching around. Owner: manager. Decision: issue an intentional walk or pitch around a hitter, a few times per week. Cases: every base-out state with first base open league-wide each season, in public play-by-play. Outcome: run expectancy and win-probability change through the end of the inning. Baseline: walk the dangerous hitter with first base open late in close games. Intervention: a matchup-specific win-probability comparison using the projected on-deck hitter and pitcher splits.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/34",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Criterion (c) likely fails because there are few decisions per club and small per-decision value. The league-wide count may support testing, while the club-level season value stays modest.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/35",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_intentional_walk_frequency",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/36",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Infield-in and positioning with a runner on third. Owner: manager and infield coach. Decision: play the infield in, halfway or back with a runner on third and fewer than two outs, multiple times per series. Cases: every such state league-wide each season, with public fielder starting positions from tracking. Outcome: run scored or prevented and extra hits allowed. Baseline: infield in late in close games, back otherwise. Intervention: a run-value threshold by batter batted-ball profile, runner speed, inning and score.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/37",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Positioning restrictions limit options, so the decision set is narrower than before rule changes.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/38",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "This may overlap with the explored outfield-positioning family in method but not in decision.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/39",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "public_fielder_positioning_data_granularity",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
