    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/40",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Level promotion timing in player development. Owner: farm director and development staff. Decision: promote, hold or demote a minor leaguer between levels, many times per season across a system. Cases: every level change across all affiliated systems each season, visible in public transaction logs. Outcome: next-level performance, injury and later MLB arrival. Baseline: promote after a fixed time or performance threshold at the current level. Intervention: a promotion-readiness model using public batted-ball and plate-discipline data and age-relative-to-level.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/41",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "This is distinct from MLB call-up translation, but outcomes are confounded because better players get promoted. That needs causal methods such as comparing near-threshold cases.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/42",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Minor-league tracking data may be inconsistent in public sources across levels and seasons, which weakens (d).",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/43",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Criterion (c) may fail because the payoff arrives years later and is hard to attribute to a single season.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
