    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/53",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Rest-day scheduling for position players and catchers. Owner: manager and performance staff. Decision: rest or start each regular, daily. Cases: every regular's starts and rest days league-wide each season in public box scores. Outcome: subsequent performance, injury list placements, and the replacement's performance. Baseline: fixed rest cadence, day games after night games. Intervention: a fatigue proxy from public sprint speed and bat speed drift triggering targeted rest.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/54",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "This differs from the explored travel and rest planning family only if the focus is in-game physical decline signals, not schedule structure, so it may be redundant.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/55",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Injury causation is not observable, which makes (b) partial.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/56",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "public_bat_speed_sprint_speed_daily_granularity",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/57",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Across all families, league-wide case counts help (a). Club-specific value (c) still requires knowing how far the club's current practice is from the model's recommendation, which is private information.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/58",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Retrospective tests on public data measure league-average policy gaps, not the club's own gap.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/59",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "In-game decisions such as sends, steals, hooks, relievers and pinch-hits likely satisfy (a) and (b) best. Development decisions such as promotions and role conversions likely fail (b) and (c) on time horizon.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0/claim/60",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/0",
