      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "verified_public_data_sources_for_each_family",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Third-base coach send/hold. Owner: third-base coach and baserunning coordinator. Decision: send or hold a runner on a ball in play, made several times per game. Historical cases: many league-wide each season in public play-by-play and tracking data, though selection bias exists because only executed outcomes are seen. Observable outcome: runner safe or out at the plate, and the base-out state afterward. Simple baseline: the coach's judgment from runner speed and the fielder's arm. Intervention: a pre-game card plus a postgame audit that scores each send against a run-expectancy breakeven, using public sprint speed, fielder arm strength, fielder distance and the game state.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/2",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Public tracking covers enough of the ball-in-play geometry (fielder position, ball location at pickup) to estimate the counterfactual safe probability of held runners, not only sent ones.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The coach can absorb a per-opponent card fast enough for a decision made in about two seconds. If not, (d) holds but the tool has no channel to change the decision.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Value per decision is small, so the season total meets (c) only if the club's current errors are systematic rather than random.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/5",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_current_send_policy",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/6",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "public_availability_of_fielder_pickup_coordinates",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Starting pitcher removal timing. Owner: manager and pitching coach. Decision: whether to pull the starter before the next batter, made at several decision points in every game. Historical cases: many each season league-wide at the batter level. Observable outcome: run value allowed by the starter's next batter versus the reliever who replaced him, though the counterfactual is unobserved. Simple baseline: pitch-count or times-through-order rule. Intervention: batter-by-batter removal guidance using public in-game velocity and command decay, the platoon matchup and the bullpen state.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "In-game velocity and release decay in public data predicts next-batter outcomes beyond pitch count. This is a testable hypothesis, not established.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/9",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Failure on (b) is partial. Removal decisions are confounded because managers pull pitchers who look worse, so retrospective tests need careful matching.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/10",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Injury-risk and next-start effects of pitcher workload are not observable in public outcome data, which caps the tool's measured value.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/11",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_pitcher_hook_rule",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/12",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "magnitude_of_confounding_in_public_removal_data",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/13",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Reliever selection by leverage and matchup. Owner: manager. Decision: which available reliever enters, and when, made one to four times per game. Historical cases: many reliever appearances each season league-wide. Observable outcome: runs allowed and win-probability change during the appearance. Simple baseline: fixed roles (closer, setup, middle) assigned by inning. Intervention: matching relievers to leverage and to the specific upcoming hitters, using public pitch-type splits and recent workload.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/14",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Overlaps the explored \"opposing bullpen availability forecast\" family only on the opponent side. Own-bullpen deployment is treated here as distinct.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/15",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Relievers' preferences for fixed roles and their readiness routines are real constraints that public data cannot capture.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/16",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Small-sample batter-versus-pitcher splits are noise. Value would come from pitch-type and handedness models, not head-to-head history.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/17",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_bullpen_role_policy",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/18",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Stolen-base and pickoff tactics under the pitch-clock and disengagement rules. Owner: first-base coach, baserunners, catcher and pitchers. Decision: attempt a steal or not, and on defense, when to use disengagements. Both occur many times per season. Historical cases: many attempts and disengagements league-wide each season under the current rules. Observable outcome: safe or caught, plus runner advancement. Simple baseline: steal with the fastest runners or when a fixed success-rate threshold is met. Intervention: attempt guidance that accounts for the pitcher's time to plate, the catcher's pop time, the disengagement count and the game state.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/19",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Rule changes split the historical sample. Only seasons under the current disengagement rules are comparable, which weakens (a).",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/20",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Opponents adapt quickly, so any edge may decay within a season.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/21",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "rule_regime_seasons_comparable",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/22",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "public_pitcher_time_to_plate_coverage",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/23",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Pinch-hitting, pinch-running and defensive replacements. Owner: manager and bench coach. Decision: which bench player to use and when, made in many games. Historical cases: many substitutions league-wide each season. Observable outcome: plate-appearance result, plus later defensive or baserunning events. Simple baseline: the platoon-advantage rule and a late-inning defensive-replacement habit. Intervention: a substitution plan that values the option of saving bench players, and the player removed, against an immediate platoon gain.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/24",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The value of a substitute who is never used is hard to observe after the fact, which weakens (b) for \"save the bench\" decisions.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/25",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "For a single club, roster construction limits how many bench options exist, so (c) may be small.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/26",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_bench_usage_pattern",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/27",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Rest-day allocation for position players. Owner: manager and performance staff. Decision: which regular sits on a given day, made many times per season. Historical cases: many rest days league-wide each season. Observable outcome: the replacement's performance that day and the rested player's performance afterward. Simple baseline: fixed rest cadences, plus sitting players against tough opposing starters or before day games after night games. Intervention: scheduling rest on days when the gap between the regular and the replacement is smallest given the opposing pitcher, park and schedule.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/28",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Fatigue and injury effects of rest are mostly unobservable in public data. Only the matchup component is testable, which weakens (b).",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/29",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Overlaps the explored \"travel and rest planning\" family. This idea is distinct only if limited to daily matchup-cost minimization.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/30",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_rest_policy",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/31",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Minor-league level-to-level promotion timing (player development). Owner: farm director. Decision: when to move a prospect up one level, made many times per season across affiliates. Historical cases: many promotions league-wide each season, with public minor-league stats. Observable outcome: the player's performance at the new level and whether he is later demoted back. Simple baseline: promote after a fixed time at the level or after a statistical threshold such as OPS or K-BB rate. Intervention: a promotion-readiness model that adjusts for age relative to the league, park, league environment and the public minor-league tracking data where it exists.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/32",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Distinct from the explored \"minor league call-up translation\" family only if limited to intra-minor-league moves.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/33",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Fails partly on (c). Value is long-run and indirect, so it does not add up within one season.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/34",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Fails partly on (b). Development outcomes are confounded by instruction quality and the organization's roster needs.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/35",
