    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/37",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Waiver claims and DFA-pool acquisitions. Owner: front office pro scouting. Decision: claim or pass on players placed on waivers or designated for assignment, made many times per season. Historical cases: many transactions league-wide each season, though claims are limited by waiver priority. Observable outcome: the claimed player's subsequent MLB performance and roster cost. Simple baseline: claim players with recent MLB time and fit for a roster need. Intervention: a ranking based on public pitch-level and batted-ball quality indicators to flag claims undervalued by surface stats.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/38",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Fails on (a) for testing claim decisions by one club, because waiver priority and counterparties limit which claims succeed. It passes for league-wide tests of player-quality prediction.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/39",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "It may resemble the explored \"minor-league free agent triage\" result, where the model tied a rule based on prior MLB time, so the ceiling could be similarly low.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/40",
