      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_waiver_priority_history",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/41",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Defensive alignment within current shift rules (infield in or back, corner depth, outfield depth outside the Wrigley wind context). Owner: defensive coordinator. Decision: positioning on each pitch or batter, so many cases per game. Historical cases: very many league-wide in public positioning data. Observable outcome: whether the batted ball becomes an out, and the run value. Simple baseline: standard positioning charts by batter spray tendency. Intervention: positioning that is conditioned on the game state (for example, infield-in breakeven calculations) and on the pitcher's tendencies.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/42",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Overlaps the explored \"Wrigley wind outfield positioning\" family. This idea is distinct only for infield and game-state alignment.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/43",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The edges may already be competed away league-wide, which would undermine (d).",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/44",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "public_positioning_data_granularity",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/45",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Intentional walks and sacrifice bunts. Owner: manager. Decision: occasional, made multiple times per week. Historical cases: many league-wide each season, though decreasing. Observable outcome: change in run expectancy and win probability. Simple baseline: the manager's convention, or a published run-expectancy table. Intervention: a game-state-specific breakeven calculation that accounts for the batter, the on-deck hitter and the pitcher.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/46",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Fails on (c). These decisions are now rare and each has small value, so the season total is likely modest.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/47",
