      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_current_iBB_bunt_frequency",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/48",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Across all ideas, (d) is the weakest criterion. Public data is also available to the other 29 clubs, so an edge requires underuse by the Cubs specifically, which is not established.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1/claim/49",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/1",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "cubs_internal_tools_already_in_use",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/1",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Starter removal timing; owner manager and pitching coach; decision is whether to pull the starter before the next batter, made several times per game in every game; historical cases are every batter faced by a starter in public pitch-by-pitch data, many thousands per season league-wide; observable outcome is run expectancy change over the rest of the inning and the following innings; simple baseline is a pitch-count or times-through-the-order threshold; intervention is a pre-batter estimate combining fatigue signals (velocity and spin drift, release-point drift, recent command), the specific upcoming hitters, and which relievers are available.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/2",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Public velocity and release-point drift within a game carries signal about the next few batters beyond what pitch count and times through the order already capture.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/3",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The counterfactual is confounded because managers pulled starters when they already saw trouble, so a retrospective test needs matched or instrumented comparisons, not raw outcome comparisons.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/4",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Criterion (c) may fail because a few runs saved per season could fall within noise for one club, even when league-wide statistical power under (a) is high.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/5",
