      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/7",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Reliever assignment by leverage and matchup; owner manager and bullpen coach; decision is which reliever enters and when, made in most games; historical cases are every relief entry league-wide in public play-by-play, many thousands per season; observable outcome is win probability added from entry to exit; simple baseline is fixed bullpen roles (closer, setup, middle relief); intervention is a pre-entry ranking that weights upcoming hitter handedness and pitch-type weakness, three-batter-minimum exposure, reliever rest, and preserving high-leverage arms for later innings.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/8",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Fixed roles leave value unused, and that value is not already captured by clubs that informally deviate from roles.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/9",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Because of the three-batter minimum, the tool has to score a pitcher against the next three or more hitters plus likely pinch hitters, not against a single matchup.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/10",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Criterion (b) partly fails because reliever availability and soreness are private, so a public retrospective will mislabel some decisions as errors when the pitcher was actually unavailable.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/11",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "reliever_availability_ground_truth",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/12",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Pinch-hit and platoon substitutions; owner manager; decision is whether to pinch-hit or start a platoon partner, made in most games; historical cases are every plate appearance where a bench bat was available, many thousands per season league-wide; observable outcome is plate-appearance run value plus the later defensive and bench-depletion cost; simple baseline is a handedness platoon rule; intervention is an estimate of the platoon split using shrinkage toward population splits, combined with a cost for losing the bench player later and for the defensive downgrade.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/13",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Individual platoon splits are noisy enough that a shrinkage model differs meaningfully from both raw splits and a pure handedness rule.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/14",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Criterion (c) may fail if the per-decision edge is small and the decisions are infrequent for a single roster.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/15",
