      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Stolen base attempts and baserunner sends; owner first-base and third-base coaches and the manager; decision is whether to attempt a steal, or send a runner home or to third on a hit, made many times per game; historical cases are every runner-on-base opportunity and every ball in play with a runner advancing, very numerous in public tracking and play-by-play data; observable outcome is safe or out plus the run expectancy change; simple baseline is a runner-speed threshold, or coach judgment proxied by league send rates; intervention is a pre-pitch or in-play probability model using sprint speed, pitcher time to plate, catcher pop time, fielder arm strength, and ball location and exit speed.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2/claim/17",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "The pickoff and disengagement limits and the larger bases changed the break-even steal rate, and some clubs' rules have not fully adjusted.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
