      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Infield and outfield positioning within the shift restrictions; owner defensive coordinator; decision is the positioning set per batter and pitcher pairing, made on every batter; historical cases are every ball in play with fielder starting positions, many thousands per season where public positioning data exists; observable outcome is out or hit and the run value of each ball in play; simple baseline is league-default or spray-chart-average positioning; intervention is positioning that conditions on the pitcher's likely pitch mix and location, the count, and the runners.",
