      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/baseline/0/2",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Intentional walks, infield-in and bunt decisions; owner manager; decision is a set of tactical calls made several times per game; historical cases are every base-out-score state where the option existed, very numerous league-wide; observable outcome is run expectancy and win probability change; simple baseline is generic run-expectancy tables or traditional rules; intervention is a state-plus-matchup model that accounts for the specific hitter, the on-deck hitter, the pitcher's walk and ground-ball tendencies, and the game state.",
