      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Position-player rest-day scheduling; owner manager and performance staff; decision is who sits on a given day, made daily; historical cases are every player-game league-wide where a regular sat or played, many thousands per season; observable outcome is short-term performance and later injured-list placement; simple baseline is a fixed rest cadence or rest tied to day games after night games; intervention is scheduling that targets low-value days (opposing starter matchup, travel, park) for rest, plus public workload signals such as sprint-speed decline.",
