      "text": "Third-base coach send/hold decisions; owner is the third-base coach with an advance and analytics staff; the decision comes up in nearly every game whenever a runner could try for home on a single or fly ball; league-wide historical cases number in the thousands per season through public play-by-play and tracking feeds; the observable outcome is safe, out, or held and the scoring that followed; the simple baseline is the coach's judgment plus a fixed rule like \"send with two outs\"; the intervention is a pregame card estimating break-even send probability by out, score, inning, runner sprint speed, fielder arm strength and fielder distance.",
