      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Starting pitcher removal timing; owner is the manager and pitching coach; the decision comes up every game, with several candidate moments per start; league-wide cases number in the thousands of starts per season, each with many decision points, in public pitch-by-pitch data; the observable outcome is run expectancy change after the pull or stay, plus later reliever workload; the simple baseline is a pitch-count or times-through-order rule; the intervention is a live estimate of the starter's current effectiveness from velocity, release and command drift compared with the specific available reliever.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
