      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Daily lineup rest-day selection for position players; owner is the manager with the performance staff; the decision comes up daily across a 162-game season; league-wide cases number in the thousands of player-days rested or played per season through public lineup cards; the observable outcome is next-game and next-week batted-ball quality, sprint speed trends, and later injured-list placements; the simple baseline is a fixed rest cadence or day-game-after-night-game rule; the intervention is a fatigue signal from public sprint speed, bat speed and exit velocity trends that suggests which days to rest.",
