      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "(b) partly fails because the benefit of rest for injury prevention is not observable at the play level and is confounded by unreported minor injuries.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5/claim/23",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "(c) may be small per game, though it adds up across a season; that is the hypothesis to test, not a given.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5/claim/24",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "whether public lineups distinguish planned rest from undisclosed injury",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5/claim/25",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem=intentional walks and unintentional-intentional pitch-around choices; owner=manager and pitching coach; decision=walk or pitch to a batter with a base open, faced several times per week; historical cases=every base-open, late-leverage plate appearance league-wide, with the choice inferable for automatic walks and approximately inferable from pitch location for pitch-arounds; outcome=play result and win-probability change, public; baseline=walk dangerous hitters with first base open late in close games; intervention=a matchup-specific run-expectancy comparison using the next hitter's projection and the platoon state.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5/claim/26",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "(c) likely fails because public research suggests these decisions carry little value per case, and clubs may have converged on them already; that claim needs verification and is not supplied here.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5/claim/27",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "Labeling pitch-arounds from pitch location adds measurement error that could swamp a small effect.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5/claim/28",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "UNKNOWN",
      "text": "league-wide frequency of automatic intentional walks since the automatic walk rule was adopted",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5/claim/29",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "IDEA",
      "text": "Problem=bullpen warm-ups that are not followed by an appearance; owner=manager and bullpen coach; decision=whether to get a reliever up, made in most close games; outcome=reliever fatigue and next-day effectiveness; baseline=warm up the next reliever when the pitcher on the mound reaches a pitch count or allows baserunners; intervention=a warm-up trigger model.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5/claim/30",
      "candidate_id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5",
      "kind": "ASSUMPTION",
      "text": "This is included as a deliberate failure case, because (b) fails: warm-up events and pitch counts are not reliably public, so a retrospective test lacks labels even though (a) and (c) may hold.",
      "status": "UNVERIFIED",
      "extractor": "line_grammar/v1"
    },
    {
      "id": "hd-20261009-212841-eccdc1b3971d/candidates/0/5/claim/31",
